# Line endings: LF, in the index and in the working tree alike.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so it checks
# files out as CRLF. Everything that writes files here — render_quizzes.py,
# sync_notebooks.py, build_css.py, myst — emits LF, so a regenerated file is
# reported as modified by `git status` forever while `git diff` shows nothing:
# the bytes are identical, only the line-ending git expects on checkout differs.
# All 175 tracked blobs are already LF-only, so this renormalizes nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: no conversion, no text diff. None of these are tracked today
# (content/*/media/ is generated and gitignored), but a rendered animation or
# an extracted frame that does get committed must not be line-ended.
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
